    {
      "Id": 1030,
      "CategoryId": 5,
      "Title": "Aloo and cap. curry",
      "Ingredients": "A dry dish made with baby potatoes and green bell peppers (Capsicum), this tastes yummy with chapatis or naans.*Ingredients:*1/4 kg baby potatoes, washed, peeled*1 large bell pepper, cut into thin long strips*12 cloves garlic, chopped*1 tsp mustard seeds*1 tsp cumin seeds*5 green chillies, chopped*1/2 tsp turmeric powder*1 tsp dhania powder*1 tsp cumin powder*1 tsp amchoor (Mango powder)*Salt to taste*5 tbsp cooking oil",
      "Method": "*In a pan pour oil and fry bell pepper and keep aside.*Heat the oil and add the cumin, mustard, green chillies and garlic.*When the mustard splutters, add the potatoes and continue frying on a high flame for about 10 minutes.*Add in the turmeric, amchoor, dhania and cumin powders and mix well.*Continue frying on a lower heat setting for about 2 more minutes.*Now sprinkle some water and cook covered on a low flame.*Do not add too much water.*Check the potatoes frequently and add water only of necessary.*Add the fried bel peppers and mix well.*Remove when potatoes are cooked.",
      "Notes": "",
      "Images": null,
      "CreatedOn": "0001-01-01T00:00:00",
      "UpdatedOn": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"
    },
