    {
      "Id": 572,
      "CategoryId": 10,
      "Title": "Apple Sambar",
      "Ingredients": "2 apples (sour)*sambar powder 4 spoons*asafetida*1 onion cut into slices*1 green chilly*1 tomato; chopped*1 cup cooked toor dhal*¼ sp dry fried and powdered fenugreek*½ sp oil (you can avoid this)",
      "Method": "Peel off the apples and cut into cubes.*Cook them with dal.*Pour 1/2 oil in a pan, add mustard, cumin.*Fry onions till they turn brown. Add green chilies.*Add the cut tomatoes and fry well.*Add the cooked dhal & apple.*Add fenugreek powder and asafetida powder.*Add sambar powder and continue boiling for another 5 mins.*Add salt, coriander leaves and put the stove in sim for 10 mins.*Serve with rice. You will like this.",
      "Notes": "",
