      "Ingredients": "Same as Bisibela Bath (Type 1)",
      "Method": "Cut the vegetables which ever you select from the list and put them all with dal and rice in the cooker.*Cook them all in a same vessel. Soak tamarind and make juice from that or use puli paste.*Put a deep pan and make seasoning and fry onions*Pour tamarind water/ puli paste with 2 cups of water in that and put the ready made bisibala bath powder in that.*When it starts to boil put all the cooked items in that and add salt and mix them well*Stir continuously to avoid sticking in the walls of the pan.*After 5 or 6 minutes remove the pan from the fire*Now the tasty bisibala bath is ready to serve.",
