      "CategoryId": 5,
      "Title": "Kadi",
      "Ingredients": "1 1/2 cups Channa dal Flour (Besan) *2 spoons Red chilly powder *1 spoon ajwan *1/4 spoon Baking powder *A pinch of Asafetida powder *2 cups thick butter milk *1/2 spoon fried and grind Fenugreek powder *Or dry Fenugreek leaves *Curry leaves *Salt *Oil to fry",
      "Method": "*Take 1/2 cup Besan and mix with the thick butter milk and mix well without any lumps. *Pour it in a pan and bring it to a boil. *Add red chilly powder, fenugreek powder, Asafetida powder and salt. *Add curry leaves and let it boil for a while. *Take balance 1 cup of Besan and add ajwan, red chilly powder, salt and baking powder. *Mix well by adding water. ( let is be like pakoda dough)*Keep oil in a frying pan and make pakodas out of the prepared mixture. *Make golden brown pakodas and put them in the boiling kadi .*After putting all the pakodas bring the kadi to a boil and remove from the fire. *This is a Rajasthani dish and will be very tasty when you serve with hot chapatti.",
