      "Title": "Kamarket",
      "Ingredients": "1 cup jaggery*1 tab.sp coconut (option)*1/2 sp ghee*1/2 sp ealachi powder.*2 tab sp rice flour.",
      "Method": "In a pan, pour some water to the grated jaggery and heat it till it gets thick.*To check if it is of the right consistency, put a drop of it in some water and try to form a ball of it. *If a tough ball turns up, just through it on a vessel. *You must hear a good sound.(\"toung\" sound) then it implies the syrup is of the right consistency. *Then sim the stove and if you want to add coconut add it now.*Mix well and add ealachi powder. *In a plate spread 1 sp rice flour and pour this paagu on that.*Allow it to cool for a while.*Then try to make balls out of it with the help of balance rice flour.*That is all. *Your Kamarket is ready. Chew and enjoy.",
