      "Ingredients": "Melted butter - 2 tbsp*Milk maid - 3 tbsp (Or condensed milk - 3 tbsp + sugar 2 tbsp)*All purpose flour (or maida / wheat flour) - 4 tbsp*Baking powder - 1/8th tbsp*Milk - 3 tbsp*Essence - Optional**For Chocolate Cake*Choco powder / Ovaltine / Nesquik / Any chocolate drink - 2 tbsp*Choch chips for topping**For Banana Walnut Cake*Smashed Banana - 1*Walnut broken - handful**For Vanilla Cake*Vanilla Essence - 5ml*Tutti fruity for topping**For Coffee Cake*Instant Coffee Powder - 1/2 tbsp*Choco powder / Ovaltine / Nesquik / Any chocolate drink - 1 1/2 tbsp*Choch chips for topping",
      "Method": "Add all the ingredients one-by-one into a 350-400 ml Microwave safe mug*Use a fork to stir the mixture to ensure that there are no lumps*The consistency should be slightly thicker than dosa dough*Keep the mixture in microwave oven. The time varies depending on your microwave power setting. For 750w, 2mins 40s mins; 850w 2mins; 1000w 1min 50s.*The quantity in the mug should be just half of the mug because while microwaving, it will grow twice in size*Your cake is ready to eat. You can directly eat it from the mug using spoon, or transfer it to a plate and cut it too",
