      "Title": "Moor milakai (Curd Chilly)",
      "Ingredients": "½ hot green chilly *2 cups curd*Salt",
      "Method": "*Cut green chilies into two with out removing the head.*Or just split a little with out removing the head.*Make curd as butter milk with out adding much water.*Add salt and cut green chilies and mix well.*Keep them for two days. *But in the morning mix them well.*The third day put them in a sheet with out buttermilk in the sun light.*In the evening again put the half dried chilies in the left over butter milk.*Repeat this till all the butter milk absorbed by the chilly.*When all chilies become crispy and if you are able to break it with your fingers, store them in an airtight container.*Fry them in oil and this is a best side dish for curd rice.",
