      "Title": "Punjabi Dhai Vada",
      "Ingredients": "maa ki dal washed -250 gm*water to soak dal*onion - 1 chopped finely*ginger - small pieces – chopped*green coriander – chopped*green chillies - 2 chopped*cumin seed - 1/2 tsp*salt - 1/2 tsp*soda-bi-carb - 1/4 tsp*oil for frying*curd - 750 gm*raisins - 15-20.",
      "Method": "*Wash and soak daal in enough water to cover the dal.*Soak it for three hours. *Drain water and grind, add chopped onion, ginger, coriander-chillies-salt, cumin seed and soda. *Heat oil.*With moistened hands, make vada with daal batter into 2\" discs.*Deep fry till light brown. Drain oil, keep aside.*Soak in hot water for 2 minutes.*Press out water lightly.*Beat curds-add- salt - 1/2 tsp. cumin seeds. *Soak-raisins in water for ten minutes.*Add to the curd. *Lay vadas in a flat dish and pour curds on it, garnish with red chilli powder-chopped coriander, powdered cumin seeds.*Serve with imli chutney and extra beaten curd.*You can garnish this will kara bundi also.",
