      "Method": "Take equal quantity of Rava and rice flour and Maida. *First fry Rava well and soak it for 1/2 an hour. *After 1/2 an hour, add other two flour with this and add salt. *Mix well and make Dosas. *You can add chopped green chilies, crushed black pepper and cumin seeds to the dough. ",
      "Notes": "",
      "Images": "https://krishnaammafood.files.wordpress.com/2022/04/21-209-ravadosa3-1.jpg",
      "CreatedOn": "0001-01-01T00:00:00",
      "UpdatedOn": "2022-04-29T15:13:43.293257"
    },
    {
      "Id": 238,
      "CategoryId": 21,
      "Title": "Rava Dosa4",
      "Ingredients": "sooji / rava - 1 cup*green chilies – 4 - 5*cumin seeds - half a tsp *onions - 2 medium*coriander - a small bunch*curry leaves - a few*coconut grating - about two tbsp.(optional)*salt to taste.*Ghee to make dosas",
      "Method": "*Fry rawa like you would for upma. And allow it to cool a bit.*(I fry rawa in big quantities and store for ready use. *In fact, this prevents the rawa from getting spoilt/worms too.) *Finely chop onions, green chilies & coriander and add it to the rawa. *Add salt, cumin, curry leaves and required amount of water for dosa consistency & mix really well. *After a few minutes you will notice that the batter absorbs water and becomes thicker. *Add little more water and mix well till you get the right consistency. *When the consistency is okay, start making dosas. *Grease the tawa well. Add oil droplets to the dosa to cook it well on both sides. *When the dosa starts browning faintly in patches, you know its done.*Just pour a little ghee on the dosa (sometimes its okay to forget the calorie-count!) :)*",
      "Notes": "",
      "Images": "https://krishnaammafood.files.wordpress.com/2022/04/21-238-ravadosa4-1.jpg",
      "CreatedOn": "0001-01-01T00:00:00",
      "UpdatedOn": "2022-04-29T15:13:44.551359"
    },
