    {
      "Id": 1206,
      "CategoryId": 1,
      "Title": "Stem Soup",
      "Ingredients": "8-10 stems of spinach leaves*4-5 tender stalks of the leaves just below cauliflower*4-5 stems of Cabbage*10 - 12 stems of coriander leaves*2 -3  small sprig spring onion*1 stalk of celery*1/2\" ginger peeled and crushed*3 – 4 garlic crushed*1 tbsp. corn flour*2 - 4 dried red chilly crushed*1/2 tsp. sugar*salt to taste*pepper as per taste*1/2 tsp. oil or butter*2 1/2 cups water",
      "Method": "*Clean any fibrous threads from the stems. *Chop the them.*Heat butter in a pan. Add ginger garlic. *Fry for a minute. Add cut stems.*Stir fry till tender. Add water and bring to a boil. *Allow it to cook.*Mix corn flour in 1/2 cup cold water. *Add to soup, stirring continuously till it comes back to a boil. *Add the chilly, sugar, salt, pepper and boil till thickened like corn soup *Serve hot.",
      "Notes": "",
