      "Title": "Tomato Soup",
      "Ingredients": "4 Tomatoes*1 Onion*2 - 3 Green chilies*Salt*Black pepper*1/2 tsp. corn flour*1/2 tsp. oil (optional)*1/2 tsp. mustard seeds (optional)",
      "Method": "*Put the tomatoes in hot water and remove the skin.*Chop onions and green chilies.*Put all of them in a mixer grinder and make them like a thick juice.*In a pan make seasoning with mustard seeds and pout the thick tomato mixture in that.*Let it boil. Add corn flour with 1 spoon water and make like a paste. Add this paste in the boiling soup and mix well without lumps.*Stir continuously to avoid lumps.*Remove from the fire and transfer it to a bowl.*Sprinkle black pepper and serve.",
