    {
      "Id": 6230,
      "CategoryId": 50,
      "Title": "Veg. Biriyani gravy",
      "Ingredients": "For dry fry :*Peanuts 1 cup*Sesame seeds 2 table spoon*Dried coconut 2 – 3 table spoons **Fry in oil:*Oil 2 tea spoon*Onion 1 medium or small onion one hand full *Ginger garlic paste 1 table spoon*Or garlic 10 – 12 pods and one inch ginger *Tomato 1 medium*Fresh coriander leaves one hand full ***Other ingredients:*Oil 2 tab.spoon*Cumin seeds 1 tea spoon*Cinnamon stick 2 inches*Cardamom 5 – 6*Bay leaf 1 -2 *Red chilly powder 1 tea spoon*Turmeric powder ½ spoon*Coriander powder 2 tea spoon*Cumin powder 1 tea spoon*Garam masala powder 1 tea spoon*Salt to taste*Fresh coriander leaves one hand full ",
      "Method": "In a pan, first dry fry peanuts and then add sesame seeds. *Fry well and add coconut.*Sim the stove and fry till you get good aroma from that.*Remove from the stove and let it cool.*Again in the same pan pour some oil and put all the ingredients which are to be fried in oil.*Fry them well and keep aside.*Now first powder the dry fried items and keep aside.*Then grind the ingredients that we fired with oil.*No need to add water, because we are having onions and tomatoes. *Remove the paste and keep aside.*Now in the pan pour some oil and make seasoning with Cumin seeds,*Cinnamon stick, Cardamom, Bay leaf .*Then add the masala paste and fry well.*Let the oil comeout  of the mixture.*Keep the gas sim.*When you see the oil is coming out of the masala, add the powdered masala and mix well.*Let it fry for two more minutes.*Now start adding all the other masalas one by one.*Red chilly powder, Turmeric powder, Coriander powder, Cumin powder,Garam masala *Powder and Salt to taste.*Mix them well and allow them to cook of few minutes.**Now add one to two cups of water in it and mix well.*Mix well without lumps.*Allow it to boil and close it with a lid.*After 5 min. open and see , mix well.*And trim the salt.*Let it boil for 2 more minutes.*Put fresh coriander leaves and remove it from the fire.*Your Biryani Gravy is ready to serve.*",
      "Notes": "You can serve this gravy with any kind of pulav or biryani. Or even with chapati also",
      "Images": "",
      "CreatedOn": "2025-03-15T19:17:45.1457374Z",
      "UpdatedOn": "2025-03-15T19:17:45.1457374Z"
    },
