    {
      "Id": 6232,
      "CategoryId": 50,
      "Title": "Aval (Poha) Puli (Tamarind) Upma",
      "Ingredients": "Mustard seeds 1 table spoon*Channa dal 1 table spoon*Udad dal 1 table spoon*Red chilly 10 -12*Ground nut 2 table spoon*Oil to cook uppma*Curry leaves one handfull*Asafoetida powder 2 pinchs*Turmeric powder 1/2 spoon*Thick Aval/Poha/Beaten rice (soak in water with salt)*Tamarind one lemon size*Gingelly oil 1 table spoon (optional) ",
      "Method": "First put salt in tamarind and extract water from that. This will help us to extract all the essence from tamarind.*In a Uruli or deep pan, pour oil and make seasoning.*Then put Aval and fry well.*Then add tamarind water and mix well.*Close it with a lid and check it after 5 min.*Then sim the flame and close the lid.*Let it be for another 5 min.*Add gingelly oil to uppma.*This will give a good flavor to Uppma and also this will avoid the uppma sticking with vessel.*Again close the lid for 10 more min.*Now it is cooked, you can transfer Aval Uppma into a plate and serve with thick curd.",
      "Notes": "",
