      "Title": "Sabudhana Vada",
      "Ingredients": "A cup of Sabudhana (wask and soak for half an hour) - Squeeze and keep aside  *1/4 kg of potatoes (boil, peel and mash)*2 - 4 tablespoons of rice flour or betten rice (poha) (powder it in a mixer grinder)*One Big onion – Chop it *Ginger half spoon crushed*Green chilli – cut into small pieces 2 - 4 tsp *Half a spoon cumin*Curry leaves*Salt*Oil to fry*One tablespoon of lemon juice (if needed)*",
      "Method": "In a big bowl, put all the ingredients together. *No need to add water.*Make big big balls out of that and keep aside.*Now in a frying pan pour oil and when it is hot, take a sabudhana ball and make it like a disk / or vada.*Make a hold in the middle, it will help vada to fry in and out.*Put as much vadas as you can in the oil. *Let it fry for a while.*Then flip it. *Let it become golden brown.*When both the sides are done take it out of the oil and put it on the kitchen towel.*Your yummy sabhudhana Vada is ready to serve.*You can serve this with tomato ketchup or any chutney. *",
