      "Id": 6236,
      "CategoryId": 50,
      "Title": "Karachi halwa corn flour halwa",
      "Ingredients": "1 cup corn flour*2 1/ 4 cups sugar*1 tsp cardamom powder*150 to 200 gms ghee*1 tsp lemon juice*Orange or preferred colour*Sliced cashew and almonds one table spoon *",
      "Method": "First take a bowl and put corn flour in that.*Pout water in it and mix well without lumps.*Now in a deep pan or thick bottom vessel, pour this and switch on the stove. *This will become thick very quickly so keep string continuously. Don’t even leave it for a second. *Add two more cups of water in it and cook it well. *Totally you will need 2.5 to 3 cups of water for this.*Let it cook, keep string it.*When you feel it is cooked, add sugar in it.*Now add lemon juice also in it.*This will avoid crystallization of sugar. *Stir well it will start turning slightly glossy.*now you add ghee  by one one teaspoon.*When you add ghee, it will become glossy and transparent in colour.*Then you can reduce the flame of the gas and stir it now and then.*Meanwhile put some ghee in a plate and spread it.*So that we can put our halwa in that.*Now you can add half of the sliced nuts and cardamom powder in halwa.*After 5 min. ghee will come out of halwa and you will feel a lump some of halwa. *At this time add food colour in it and mix well.*Then transfer it in the plate and decorate the halwa with the balance sliced nuts.*Allow it for an hour.*Then cut it and serve.*Your delicious Karachi halwa is ready to eat. *",
      "Notes": "",
