      "Title": "MTR Style Rava Idly",
      "Ingredients": "Thick curd - 250 ml (mix with water )*Bombay Rava-1 cup*Panshirava - also known as sirutti rava 1 cup*A cup of chopped fresh coriander (optional)*One teaspoon of powdered sugar (optional)*Salt - required quantity*A handful of whole cashews - split into two*Oil quarter cup*ENO FRUIT SALT PLAIN 1 1/2 Table Spoon**For Seasoning:**1 teaspoon of mustard*1 teaspoon of Udad dal*1/4 teaspoon of asafetida powder*One tablespoon of crushed green chilli*A tablespoon of crushed ginger*",
      "Method": "In a big vessel put both the ravas and mix well.*In a pan put cashews and fry well.*Remove and keep aside.*Then put all the ingredients given for seasoning and make the seasoning.*Then pour it on the rava mixture and mix it well.*Now put chopped coriander and salt in it.*Mix well.*Now add curd and mix well.*The dough must be thicker than normal idly dough.*Now add Eno fruit salt in the dough and mix well.*You can see the dough is increasing because of Eno.*Then make idles as usual by putting them in the idly plates; KEEP ONE ONE CASHEW FIRST AND THEN POUR THE DOUGH.*After 10 - 12 min. open the pan and remove the idly plates.*You can see the size of the idlies.*They will be very bigger than normal; like MTR !*Enjoy the MTR STYLE RAVA IDLY WITH ANY CHUTNEY !*",
